[{"label":"Three house styles","html":"<div\n  class=\"toggle-group\"\n  role=\"group\"\n  aria-label=\"House style\"\n  data-type=\"single\"\n  id=\"ps-styles\"\n  style=\"margin: 0 auto 1rem; display: flex; justify-content: center\"\n>\n  <button class=\"toggle\" aria-pressed=\"true\" data-style=\"modern\">Modern</button>\n  <button class=\"toggle\" aria-pressed=\"false\" data-style=\"classic\">Classic</button>\n  <button class=\"toggle\" aria-pressed=\"false\" data-style=\"minimal\">Minimal</button>\n</div>\n<article class=\"paper\" id=\"ps-paper\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Short paper</span\n      ><span>defuss-shadcn · <time datetime=\"2026-10\">October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"ps-title\"\n      >Three House Styles<span class=\"paper-title-sub\">One set of parts, three ways to set them</span></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li\n      ><li>Claude</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >A research page, a journal article and a lab note share their parts: a title block, an abstract, numbered\n      sections, tables. What differs is the house style. Modern Paper keeps the parts and lets one attribute choose the\n      style, so an author can change the look of a finished paper without touching its markup.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#ps-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Modern</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#ps-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>Classic</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#ps-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>Minimal</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#ps-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Modern</h2>\n    <p\n      >The default is a project page: a centred title block, serif headings over a sans body, ruled section heads and a\n      tinted abstract with an accent edge.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>Classic</h2>\n    <p\n      >The classic style sets a printed journal: serif throughout, a narrower column set justified and hyphenated,\n      section heads in small capitals without a rule, and an abstract set in from both sides.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-s3\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>Minimal</h2>\n    <p\n      >The minimal style is a lab note: everything flush start, a sans title, the abstract under a hairline instead of a\n      tint, no rules under the heads.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"ps-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"ps-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026housestyles,\n  title = {Three House Styles: One Set of Parts, Three Ways to Set Them},\n  author = {Homberg, Aron and Claude},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-styles.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@book{bringhurst2004elements,\n  author = {Bringhurst, Robert},\n  title = {The Elements of Typographic Style},\n  edition = {3},\n  publisher = {Hartley \\& Marks},\n  address = {Vancouver},\n  year = {2004}\n}\n\n@inproceedings{park2021nerfies,\n  author = {Keunhong Park and Utkarsh Sinha and Jonathan T. Barron and Sofien Bouaziz and Dan B. Goldman and Steven M. Seitz and Ricardo Martin-Brualla},\n  title = {Nerfies: Deformable Neural Radiance Fields},\n  booktitle = {Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision},\n  pages = {5865--5874},\n  year = {2021}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
